 favor if the deal fails;\n   the 1991 lease has a 150% holdover clause. The downside is not\n   modeled by the rally.\n4. Operating margins (8.5%) are at 10-year HIGHS; the 10-yr median is\n   5.3%; mean-reversion alone brings FY28 FCF to ~$100M, not $150M.\n5. D&A ($45M) exceeds capex ($36M): the company is under-investing in\n   its owned physical plant; a maintenance catch-up ($15-20M/yr) would\n   cut FCF 10%+.\n6. The stock doubled on a press release, not a definitive agreement.\n   Short-sellers have covered (-5.3% MoM); the fuel for the squeeze is\n   spent.\n7. No sell-side target (mean not available); no formal guidance; the only\n   \"guidance\" in the market is a 402-error earnings-call excerpt \u2014\n   investors are flying blind into a binary event.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic combat (Long vs Short, 0-10 each):\n- Long case strength: 4/10 (real demographic tailwind, strong insider\n  ownership, clean balance sheet, credible activist-endgame).\n- Short case strength: 7/10 (deal math uninspiring, default weakens\n  negotiating hand, overvaluation by 2\u00d7, no guidance, no Q&A).\n- GAP = 3 > threshold 2 \u2192 CONVICTION DOWNGRADE not needed; already low.\n- Verdict: SHORT ARGUMENT DOMINATES.\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial reports: The web brief cites Land & Buildings'\n\"up to 38% EBITDA hit\" figure and the NHI proxy fight. Sources\n[Estimate]: Skilled Nursing News, WSJ, L&B, Snowball Research. None\nalleges fraud; all point to value-transfer risk in the lease repricing.\nThe Holland & Knight announcement is the sole positive \u2014 and it is a\npress release, not a definitive agreement.\n\nStep 9-4. Killed arguments (and revive conditions):\n- Killed: \"NHC will simply buy the properties at 5% cap and massively\n  accrete.\" REVIVE IF: the definitive agreement shows a price\n  below-replacement, seller-financed at \u22645.5%, with no equity dilution.\n- Killed: \"The market knows something we don't \u2014 the rally is smart\n  money.\" REVIVE IF: an 8-K with the purchase agreement is filed with\n  terms showing IRR >15% to NHC shareholders.\n- Killed: \"NHC is a Warren Buffett / undervalued compounder.\" REVIVE IF:\n  (a) ROIC > 12% for 3 years post-deal, (b) organic revenue > 6%,\n  (c) leverage returns to <2\u00d7 by FY29.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT RESULTS (37-point sample across 7 domains)\n\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\u2501\n\nA. Methodology audit \u2014 PASS. Engine chosen explicitly (Engine 2 with\n   Engine 1 cross-check); no skipped layers; no DCF-only conclusion; no\n   peer-multiple-only conclusion; no TAM-only conclusion.\nB. Valuation audit \u2014 PASS with reservations. WACC 8.75% is above the\n   7.6% a naive CAPM would give; deliberately conservative. FCF\n   definition = NOPAT + D&A \u2212 capex \u2212 \u0394WC, cross-checked with OCF\u2212capex;\n   SBC deducted explicitly.\nC. Bias audit \u2014 PASS. I owned the analysis; no pre-existing bullishness.\n   Key risk: anchoring on the +122% move may underweight the likelihood\n   that the market is correct about the deal terms I failed to retrieve.\n   Mitigated: Bear/Base/Bull scenarios carry explicit term variation.\nD. Consistency audit \u2014 FA