s cross-check)\n- **T0:** $233.40 | **IV Base (DCF):** $144 | **Scenario EV:** $176 | **MoS:** \u221232% to \u221238%\n- **Critical Tpf Event:** Completed $560M purchase of 35 NHI facilities on 2026-07-01, funded by $475M term loan + $55M revolver drawn [Actual \u2014 10-Q via StockTitan 2026-08-06]\n- **Confidence:** Medium-Low | **Opinion:** AVOID / REDUCE existing positions\n\n### Archetype Transition Determination\n- NHC historically Stable Incumbent (A); the NHI deal adds a real-estate-owner dimension, but does NOT yet satisfy Quality Compounder (B) thresholds (ROIC > WACC for 3 consecutive years). Transition criteria: 0\u201350% met \u2192 Engine 1 is correct. Repeated large acquisitions could trigger reclassification to D (Product-Platform Hybrid) or B; not yet supported.\n\n### Engine Selection Reason\n1. Reimbursement-regulated, recurring, inelastic-demand cash flows; no product optionality.\n2. Real estate ownership + facilities operation = asset-heavy, cash-generative; DCF captures owner cash flows.\n3. Alternative (Engine 2 Cyclical) rejected: SNF census is decoupled from GDP cycles (90.1% occupancy); no commodity pricing.\n4. Failed alternative would occur with Engine 4 (Expectation-Driven) \u2014 would over-reward narrative optionality that management has not demonstrated.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25