u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n### 2-1 Business Understanding (3 sentences)\nNHC operates skilled nursing, assisted living, independent living, home health and hospice services across the U.S., concentrated in Tennessee and the Southeast. It owns approximately 115+ facilities post-July-2026 (80 SNFs + 26 ALs + 35 acquired from NHI) and leases a small residual portfolio. Revenues derive from Medicare/Medicaid reimbursement plus private-pay residents, with occupancy at ~90%.\n\n**Understandability: HIGH**\n\n### 2-2 Moat Assessment (0\u20133 each)\n| Moat Component | Score | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand/licenses) | 1 | Stable |\n| Switching costs (referral relationships) | 1 | Stable |\n| Network effects | 0 | N/A |\n| Cost advantage (owned real estate, in-house insurance) | 2 | **Widening** (NHI ownership removes rent) |\n| Economies of scale | 1 | Stable |\n| Regulatory barriers (CON laws, licensure) | 2 | Stable |\n| Data moat | 0 | N/A |\n| **Total** | **7/21** | **Stable-to-Widening** |\n\n\u2192 **Narrow moat**; driven by balance-sheet conservatism rather than pricing power (research brief: NHC market share 0.86% vs HCA 43.09%) [Estimate \u2014 csimarket.com].\n\n### 2-3 Lynch Classification\n**Stalwart** \u2014 3-yr revenue CAGR 11.8% [Estimate], dividend yield 1.24% [Actual \u2014 vendor], steady operability.\nKey checkpoints: continuity of margin, no encumbrance of balance sheet, management allocation. The $560M debt move is the single largest deviation from the historical stable trajectory.\n\n### 2-4 Financial Strength Scorecard\n| Metric | Value | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue growth 3-yr CAGR (FY22\u201325) | 11.8% | [Estimate] |\n| Operating margin FY2025 | 8.4% | [Actual] |\n| Operating margin 10-yr median | 5.3% | [Actual \u2014 pack \u00a77] |\n| ROE (TTM) | 13.27% | [Actual \u2014 vendor] |\n| FCF margin (TTM) | 9.4% | [Estimate] |\n| FCF conversion (FCF/OCF) | 78% | [Estimate] |\n| Net debt post-July 2026 | $478M ($530M drawn \u2212 $52M cash) | [Actual \u2014 10-Q] |\n| Forward EBITDA / Interest | ~7.9\u00d7 ($228M / $29M) | [Estimate] |\n\n**Judgment: GOOD**, with a material new leverage constraint.\n\n### 2-5 Capital Allocation Scorecard (0\u201315)\n1. **Buyback efficiency: 1** \u2014 $23.6M H1-2026 at avg ~$172 [Actual \u2014 10-Q]; not excessive, but not deep-value multi-year.\n2. **M&A track record: 2** \u2014 small SNF purchases historically; $560M is a scale-jump with unproven integration.\n3. **Capex efficiency: 2** \u2014 prior low capex ($26\u201339M/yr) on leased model; ownership requires higher future maintenance spend.\n4. **Rationality of mix: 2** \u2014 dividends + repurchases + acquisitions balanced; but the debt-funded pivot is a strategy shift.\n5. **Guidance accuracy: 1** \u2014 no formal EPS guidance; [Unconfirmed] track record opacity.\n**Total: 8/15**\n\nInsider bonus: ownership 18.88% **+1**; recent insider net transactions [Unconfirmed].\n**Adjusted total: 9/17**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n## SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2