 50.5 + 40 + 45 \u2212 210.2 \u2248 $450M [Estimate]\nEquity value = 3,240 \u2212 450 = $2,790M\nPer share (15.661M) = $178\n\nTornado sensitivity (\u00b11\u03c3 on key drivers):\n\u2022 WACC 6.9% vs 7.9% \u2192 IV $210 vs $155 [Assumption range]\n\u2022 Terminal growth 2.5% vs 3.5% \u2192 IV $158 vs $201\n\u2022 2027 EBIT margin 8.5% vs 11.5% \u2192 IV $146 vs $211\n\u2022 Rent saved $47M vs $78M \u2192 IV $177 vs $190 (impact limited\n  because interest on the purchase offsets)\n\u2022 Maintenance capex $55M vs $80M \u2192 IV $192 vs $162\nTop 3 KPIs (become Thesis KPIs): (1) 2027 EBIT margin; (2) WACC\n\u2014 any rise in SOFR materially hurts; (3) maintenance capex\ndiscipline.\n\nCross-checks:\n\u2022 P/FFO (real-estate basis): FFO2027E \u2248 NI 178 \u00d7 0.75 + D&A 67\n  \u2248 $200M \u2192 P/FFO \u2248 20.5x at $233 [Estimate] \u2014 full REIT\n  multiple for an operator\n\u2022 EV/EBITDA 2027E: EBITDA 241M; EV 4,105M \u2192 17.0x [Estimate \u2014\n  rich vs sector 10\u201313x]\n\u2022 P/E on 2027 adjusted EPS ~$8.60 \u2192 27.1x [Estimate]\n\u2022 Reverse DCF: $233 implies 2027\u20132030 average NOPAT ~$175M and\n  terminal g ~3.5%, i.e., EBIT margin ~12% \u2014 150bp above our\n  base, achievable only with flawless integration [Assumption]\n\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 3.5-1. Competitive response: Large operators (HCA, Ensign,\nGenesis) may bid up acquisition prices for SNF portfolios,\nraising NHC's future M&A cost [Assumption]. No immediate price-\nwar risk in post-acute care.\nStep 3.5-2. Reflexivity: Positive \u2014 the deal de-risks earnings,\nenabling cheaper